[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4319657879","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118948#issuecomment-4319657879","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118948","id":4319657879,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAXi_lw","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-25T12:56:48Z","updated_at":"2026-04-25T12:56:48Z","body":"> given no earlier reports of the bug is seems that WorldBoundaryShape3D is not widely used with a `plane` with `d != 0`\r\n\r\n\"Widely used\" is hard to define obviously, but given that [this search](https://github.com/search?q=%2FWorldBoundaryShape3D.*%5Cn.*plane+%3D+Plane%5C%28-%3F%5B%5Cd.%5D%2B%2C+-%3F%5B%5Cd.%5D%2B%2C+-%3F%5B%5Cd.%5D%2B%2C+-%3F%5B%5Cd.%5D*%5B1-9%5D%5B%5Cd.%5D*%5C%29%2F&type=code) yields more than a handful of results, I wouldn't be so sure about that.\r\n\r\nThe fact that the plane debug shape very clearly goes the wrong way when using Jolt might still suggest that's the case, but I could definitely see people just not noticing and using it anyway.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4319657879/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4319752400","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118948#issuecomment-4319752400","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118948","id":4319752400,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAXow0A","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-25T13:50:38Z","updated_at":"2026-04-25T13:50:38Z","body":"> The fact that the plane debug shape very clearly goes the wrong way when using Jolt might still suggest that's the case, but I could definitely see people just not noticing and using it anyway.\r\n\r\nThey may have noticed, but also just had the same misconception as me (that it was a gizmo issue) and just ignored the gizmo and trusted the actual result, haha.\r\n\r\nAnyway, thank you for the fix!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4319752400/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4319762018","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118948#issuecomment-4319762018","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118948","id":4319762018,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAXpWYg","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-25T13:56:00Z","updated_at":"2026-04-25T13:56:00Z","body":"Ah, easy mistake to make. I've always been taught to write a plane equation as `n . x + c = 0`, [wiki](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euclidean_planes_in_three-dimensional_space) agrees with this definition :)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4319762018/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4319775175","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118948#issuecomment-4319775175","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118948","id":4319775175,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAXqJxw","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-25T14:03:19Z","updated_at":"2026-04-25T14:03:19Z","body":"> Ah, easy mistake to make. I've always been taught to write a plane equation as `n . x + c = 0`, [wiki](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Euclidean_planes_in_three-dimensional_space) agrees with this definition :)\r\n\r\nThis is what I was taught as well! I'll admit I didn't even know the other form was acceptable until now. That said, regardless of what I considered to be the mathematical \"standard\", I do find it more _intuitive_ to think about d as going up along the normal like in Godot. It always bothered me in Unity having to invert my thinking.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4319775175/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4319931681","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118948#issuecomment-4319931681","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118948","id":4319931681,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAXztIQ","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-25T15:17:36Z","updated_at":"2026-04-25T15:17:36Z","body":"Can we make this a new project setting that defaults to the old behavior if not set, the new behavior if set? And set it by default on new projects?\r\n\r\nThis seems like a footgun big enough to maybe try to help the users a little? 😅","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4319931681/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4320522980","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118948#issuecomment-4320522980","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118948","id":4320522980,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAYXy5A","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-25T20:47:22Z","updated_at":"2026-04-25T20:47:22Z","body":"> Can we make this a new project setting that defaults to the old behavior if not set, the new behavior if set? And set it by default on new projects?\r\n> \r\n> This seems like a footgun big enough to maybe try to help the users a little? 😅\r\n\r\nI feel like this is a thing that's so wrong, it shouldn't be an option. If `WorldBoundaryShape3D` had its own `offset` or `distance` property, I might understand, but the fact is that it uses Godot's core `Plane` class directly as its `plane` property. This means that, if you're using Jolt, and you take that `plane` property and call its functions like `intersects_ray` or `has_point` or `distance_to`, you'll get results that completely mismatch the physics engine's behaviour. It's too internally inconsistent to be a harmless \"alternate convention\".","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4320522980/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4320597554","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118948#issuecomment-4320597554","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118948","id":4320597554,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAYcWMg","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-25T21:27:53Z","updated_at":"2026-04-25T21:27:53Z","body":"\r\n> I feel like this is a thing that's so wrong, it shouldn't be an option. If `WorldBoundaryShape3D` had its own `offset` or `distance` property, I might understand, but the fact is that it uses Godot's core `Plane` class directly as its `plane` property. This means that, if you're using Jolt, and you take that `plane` property and call its functions like `intersects_ray` or `has_point` or `distance_to`, you'll get results that completely mismatch the physics engine's behaviour. It's too internally inconsistent to be a harmless \"alternate convention\".\r\n\r\nI didn't think it was a harmless alternate convention, I mean that because it isn't I'm worried about the number of existing games breaking.\r\n\r\nMy suggestion was purely to not change behavior for existing projects, but letting them opt in to the fix. \r\n\r\nThis just seemed like a really hard to debug breakage if someone made the previous behavior work for them.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4320597554/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4320645229","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118948#issuecomment-4320645229","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118948","id":4320645229,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAYfQbQ","user":{"login":"MajorMcDoom","id":13228932,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjI4OTMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13228932?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom","html_url":"https://github.com/MajorMcDoom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MajorMcDoom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-25T21:48:29Z","updated_at":"2026-04-25T21:48:29Z","body":"> > I feel like this is a thing that's so wrong, it shouldn't be an option. If `WorldBoundaryShape3D` had its own `offset` or `distance` property, I might understand, but the fact is that it uses Godot's core `Plane` class directly as its `plane` property. This means that, if you're using Jolt, and you take that `plane` property and call its functions like `intersects_ray` or `has_point` or `distance_to`, you'll get results that completely mismatch the physics engine's behaviour. It's too internally inconsistent to be a harmless \"alternate convention\".\r\n> \r\n> I didn't think it was a harmless alternate convention, I mean that because it isn't I'm worried about the number of existing games breaking.\r\n> \r\n> My suggestion was purely to not change behavior for existing projects, but letting them opt in to the fix.\r\n> \r\n> This just seemed like a really hard to debug breakage if someone made the previous behavior work for them.\r\n\r\nAn opt-in fix means the default is wrong for everyone else. Whatever likelihood of users not catching this breaking change, there is even more likelihood of other users not knowing that they have to check a box for things to work correctly.\r\n\r\nAs I've pointed out, the current behaviour can also create bugs too, which arguably are more difficult to debug. Breaking changes are documented and should be checked before updating. But even if you miss it, it means if you go to investigate the issue, you'll notice the gizmo now correctly reflects the underlying physics. It seems like a trivial fix.\r\n\r\nEither way, I'm not super familiar with how Godot handles breaking changes and backward compatibility, so I'll let the team figure this one out. But those are just my two cents. :)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4320645229/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4320661052","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118948#issuecomment-4320661052","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118948","id":4320661052,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAYgOPA","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-25T21:53:35Z","updated_at":"2026-04-25T21:53:35Z","body":"I just double checked and that `to_jolt` function is currently only used by the `WorldBoundaryShape3D`, so only that is affected by this change at the moment (so no ray casts etc.). But I agree with @MajorMcDoom that it should be fixed without a project setting:\r\n\r\n* Having the project setting would also mean that everyone with an existing project that starts to use a `WorldBoundaryShape3D` for the first time will get a broken shape and will have to spend time figuring out that there is a project setting. \r\n* It doesn't make sense to have more than a few `WorldBoundaryShape3D` objects in a game so there shouldn't be much content to fix. \r\n* It will be pretty obvious if the floor is in the wrong spot.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4320661052/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4320705104","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118948#issuecomment-4320705104","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118948","id":4320705104,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAYi6UA","user":{"login":"rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229837?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing","html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-25T22:22:39Z","updated_at":"2026-04-28T07:50:45Z","body":"I just want to point out that the `plane` property of WorldBoundaryShape3D could be deprecated since it's redundant with e.g. transforming the collision shape node (more generally, whenever a shape resource is used, there is usually a separately stored transform to apply to the shape, in all of the physics API if I'm not mistaken). Setting the `plane` property with a nonzero distance (or more strictly, a value not equal to the default) could print an error. Maybe a bit drastic, but it would help migration.\r\n\r\nEdit: Here's an example of that kind of approach:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/fd8c4ef3e982b9e6973c858f6c3354abc1331b6a/scene/gui/tab_container.cpp#L833-L844","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4320705104/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4322764684","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118948#issuecomment-4322764684","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118948","id":4322764684,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAagnjA","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-26T19:01:23Z","updated_at":"2026-04-26T19:01:23Z","body":"> An opt-in fix means the default is wrong for everyone else. Whatever likelihood of users not catching this breaking change, there is even more likelihood of other users not knowing that they have to check a box for things to work correctly.\r\n\r\nI only mean it to be opt-in for EXISTING projects. New projects should get the new and correct behavior.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4322764684/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4322798798","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118948#issuecomment-4322798798","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118948","id":4322798798,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAaiszg","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-26T19:15:12Z","updated_at":"2026-04-26T19:15:12Z","body":"> I only mean it to be opt-in for EXISTING projects. New projects should get the new and correct behavior.\r\n\r\nI understand, but EXISTING projects that start using the `WorldBoundaryShape3D` object for the first time will be placing broken versions of that shape. The gizmo will be wrong and if you set `d` through a script it does the opposite of what the documentation states. Imo this causes an equal amount of confusion and it will not be obvious that you have to change a project setting to fix it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4322798798/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4333562095","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118948#issuecomment-4333562095","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118948","id":4333562095,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAkzo7w","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-28T08:26:53Z","updated_at":"2026-04-28T08:26:53Z","body":"> > I only mean it to be opt-in for EXISTING projects. New projects should get the new and correct behavior.\r\n> \r\n> I understand, but EXISTING projects that start using the `WorldBoundaryShape3D` object for the first time will be placing broken versions of that shape. The gizmo will be wrong and if you set `d` through a script it does the opposite of what the documentation states. Imo this causes an equal amount of confusion and it will not be obvious that you have to change a project setting to fix it.\r\n\r\nI'm just not sure if it's more confusing if it's wrong immediately vs upgrading a project that has existed suddenly changing behavior.\r\n\r\nWe could maybe print a warning? \r\n\r\nI'm just concerned because Unity users tend to really, really dread engine upgrades. Godot users generally don't. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4333562095/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4336034568","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118948#issuecomment-4336034568","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118948","id":4336034568,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAnKjCA","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-28T14:14:48Z","updated_at":"2026-04-28T14:14:48Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4336034568/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":3,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]